.TH MM-DESK 1 "November 20, 2026" "MM Desk CLI 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mm-desk \- interactive client for the mm_pool_desk API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mm-desk
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mm-desk
.RI [ options ]
.BI \-c " command"
.RB [ \-c " command ..."]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mm-desk
connects to a desk over WebSocket and provides an interactive command prompt.
It supports authentication, orders, balances, history, withdrawals,
and TWAP/VWAP schedules.
.PP
At the prompt,
.B help
lists commands and
.B help COMMAND
shows a command's options.
For API commands,
.B COMMAND \-\-help
also displays usage without executing the command.
The
.B manual
command opens this page with the system
.BR man (1)
viewer.
The viewer selects its normal pager and respects the user's pager
configuration.
With
.BR less (1),
Space advances a page, / searches, n repeats a search, and q returns to the
CLI.
.PP
Without a terminal, output can be redirected or piped using normal shell
rules.
The CLI does not implement its own pager or print Markdown source as help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Display startup usage and exit successfully without connecting.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-manual
Open this manual with man(1), without connecting.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Desk WebSocket endpoint. Overrides MM_DESK_URL.
Default: wss://desk.testnet.curated.finance.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed-file " FILE"
Authenticate at startup using a hexadecimal Ed25519 desk seed.
.TP
.BI \-\-master-file " FILE"
Derive a desk seed and chain owner from an mm-keys.py master seed,
then authenticate. Mutually exclusive with --seed-file.
.TP
.BI \-\-owner " ADDRESS"
Associate this chain owner with automatic login. Requires a seed or master
file.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Positive finite request timeout. Default: 15.
.TP
.BI \-\-latency-log " FILE"
Append order request timings as JSONL. Default:
$XDG_STATE_HOME/mm-desk/latency.jsonl, or
~/.local/state/mm-desk/latency.jsonl if XDG_STATE_HOME is unset or relative.
.TP
.B \-\-no-proxy
Disable automatic WebSocket proxy use. HTTP chain queries use urllib's
normal proxy settings.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Skip the startup desk connection. Explicit chain queries remain available.
Cannot be combined with automatic login.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start a local protocol simulator with a public test key.
Cannot be combined with a URL, MM_DESK_URL, login options, or --offline.
.TP
.BR \-c , " \-\-command " COMMAND
Execute one interactive command and exit. May be repeated for a sequence
within the same connection. Processing stops on an error or business
rejection.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B connect [URL]
Connect or reconnect. Omitting URL reuses the previous endpoint.
Reconnecting clears authentication and requires login again.
.TP
.B disconnect
Close the connection and clear local authentication.
.TP
.B login [--seed-file FILE | --master-file FILE] [--owner ADDRESS]
Obtain a challenge, sign it, and authenticate. Without a file, read a desk
seed with input hidden. Non-interactive login requires a file.
.TP
.B pubkey [--seed-file FILE | --master-file FILE]
Derive the public API key locally without logging in.
.TP
.B check-balance [ADDRESS | --owner ADDRESS] [--rpc-url URL] [--limit N] [--json]
With an address, query that chain owner in any connection state.
Without an address after login, query both the desk and linked chain owner.
Before login, an omitted address prompts interactively; non-interactive
queries require an address. The default chain endpoint is
https://rpc.testnet.curated.finance and the default leaf limit is 1000.
.TP
.B chain-balances
Alias for check-balance, with the same options.
.TP
.B rpc METHOD [JSON | @FILE]
Call a JSON-RPC method. Omitted params are an empty object. Known methods
validate parameters and fill omitted timestamps; unknown methods receive
the object as supplied. Raw JSON does not translate token names.
.TP
.B status
Show the connection, desk account, scopes, linked chain owner and source,
and ignored-message count.
.TP
.B now
Print current Unix milliseconds.
.TP
.B help [COMMAND]
Show commands or the selected command's options. ? and methods are aliases.
.TP
.B manual
Open this page with man(1). Reading the manual keeps the WebSocket event
loop running. Use help COMMAND for a short command reference.
.TP
.B quit
Exit and close the connection. exit is an alias. Ctrl-D and Ctrl-C also exit.
Exit does not submit cancellations.
.SH ORDER REQUEST LATENCY
place, batch, modify, cancel, cancel-all, algo-place, and algo-cancel
print TTL (RTT) in milliseconds to standard error when a request completes.
Full method names and raw rpc calls have the same behavior.
One batch has one RTT for the entire request.
.PP
A monotonic clock measures from immediately before WebSocket send until the
matching response arrives. RTT includes network transit and desk processing;
it excludes local validation, JSON serialization, log writes, and display.
It does not measure subsequent execution or settlement.
Rejections and RPC errors also have RTTs. Without a matching response,
timeouts and connection failures print an unavailable RTT and elapsed wait.
Requests rejected locally before sending are not timed. No request is retried.
.PP
One JSONL record is appended per completed request. Records contain a UTC
timestamp, run ID, sanitized endpoint, account and request IDs, method,
order/request references, outcome, rtt_ms, and elapsed_ms.
rtt_ms is null when no matching response arrives.
Credentials and full payloads are excluded. A log-write failure reports a
warning without changing the request result.
.PP
The interactive banner shows the log path. The default is
$XDG_STATE_HOME/mm-desk/latency.jsonl, falling back to
~/.local/state/mm-desk/latency.jsonl. Override it with --latency-log FILE.
The file is created on first use with mode 0600 and appended across restarts.
.SH TRANSFERS
.B transfer to-desk
.B (--key-file FILE | --master-file FILE)
.B --token TOKEN (--amount DECIMAL | --raw-amount INTEGER)
.RI [ options ]
.PP
Deposit from the linked chain account into the desk pool through the spot
contract's deposit_pool command. The chain key must match the owner linked
to the current login. Environment parameters come from desk_networks.json.
Ordinary transfers to the pool owner are not desk deposits.
.PP
.B transfer from-desk
.B --token TOKEN (--amount DECIMAL | --raw-amount INTEGER)
.RI [ options ]
.PP
Withdraw through mm_withdraw. Requires withdraw scope when submitting.
--to defaults to the linked chain owner and must match that owner if given.
No chain private key is required for this direction.
.PP
Both directions accept --rpc-url, --timeout, --wait-timeout, --no-wait,
--json, and mutually exclusive --yes / --dry-run. The default is preview
only. to-desk also accepts repeated --leaf inputs.
.PP
--amount is in normal token units; --raw-amount is in smallest units.
The original low-level withdraw command still uses raw --amount values.
.PP
Without --yes, to-desk runs the chain simulation and from-desk prints a
local request preview. The desk has no withdrawal simulation endpoint.
With --yes, submissions are sent once. Unless --no-wait is used, deposits
wait for chain finality then a matching mm_deposits txhash, while withdrawals
wait for their matching request and finalized payout transaction.
.PP
--wait-timeout defaults to 120 seconds for each waiting stage. A timeout
does not undo a transfer. Errors retain the transaction hash or request ID
for follow-up queries; never automatically resubmit.
.PP
Use transfer to-desk --help or transfer from-desk --help for full options.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The server supplies a challenge through mm_challenge. The client signs
the UTF-8 prefix mm_pool_desk/login: followed by the decoded challenge bytes
using the Ed25519 desk seed. mm_login sends the public API key and signature;
private seeds are processed locally.
.PP
A master seed is optional. It can derive both desk and chain keys using
the same HKDF labels as mm-keys.py. With a .desk.seed filename, a matching
sibling .master.seed may be used after verifying that it derives that desk
seed.
.PP
Chain-owner selection is: explicit login --owner, a matching master,
then the endpoint/public-key association in accounts.json.
Pasted-seed and raw login also use accounts.json.
The login API returns mm_id and scopes, not the chain owner.
A failed login, another key, or a disconnected session cannot inherit the
previous session's owner association.
.SH BALANCES
The balances command calls mm_balances for the authenticated desk account.
check-balance without an address after login displays desk and chain balances
in separate sections. An empty desk list displays "Empty (no desk balances)."
JSON mode retains the empty array. If one source fails, the other result
remains visible and the command reports failure.
.PP
An explicit chain address never changes the owner linked to the login.
Chain queries include undeleted leaves whose second index is 3, summing
the second 32-byte data word by operator. Integer arithmetic preserves
precision.
Only one page is fetched; full pages, continuation markers, and malformed
records are reported as potentially incomplete.
.PP
Chain assets do not establish available desk funds or deposit credit.
Use transfer to-desk to create a deposit_pool transaction.
.SH DATA CONVENTIONS
Prices, quantities, and amounts are decimal strings of raw on-chain integers.
Fractions and floating-point amounts are not accepted. Market scales, ticks,
minimum notionals, and execution rules are enforced by the desk.
.PP
Timestamps use Unix milliseconds. Known methods fill omitted ts values;
explicit values are preserved. The protocol requires clock skew within
five seconds. History intervals include from and exclude to.
.PP
Modify accepts quantity as a new total or remaining as a new remainder;
they cannot be supplied together. Batch accepts 1 to 50 order objects.
Withdraw requires withdraw scope and the owner's Cura account address.
.SH DESK API COMMANDS
Short commands and full mm_* method names accept the same options.
Scope "any" requires authentication; other named scopes must be granted
to the current key. Optional fields are omitted unless supplied, except
for automatic ts values.

.SS "challenge"
Get a login challenge.
.br
RPC: mm_challenge. Scope: none.
No parameters.

.SS "login-raw"
Authenticate with a public key and signature (normally use login).
.br
RPC: mm_login. Scope: none.
.TP
.B "\-\-key\-id HEX32"
Required. 32\-byte Ed25519 public key in hexadecimal.
.TP
.B "\-\-signature HEX64"
Required. 64\-byte Ed25519 signature in hexadecimal.

.SS "deadman"
Set the deadman timeout; 0 disables it.
.br
RPC: mm_setDeadman. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-timeout\-ms UINT"
Required. Deadman timeout in milliseconds; zero disables it.

.SS "gateway-token"
Get a market\-data gateway JWT.
.br
RPC: mm_gatewayToken. Scope: any.
No parameters.

.SS "place"
Place an order; price and quantity are raw on\-chain integers.
.br
RPC: mm_placeOrder. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-book STR"
Required. Order book identifier.
.TP
.B "\-\-side BUY|SELL"
Required. buy or sell.
.TP
.B "\-\-price AMOUNT"
Required. Raw integer price.
.TP
.B "\-\-quantity AMOUNT"
Required. Raw integer total quantity.
.TP
.B "\-\-tif GTC|IOC"
Required. gtc or ioc.
.TP
.B "\-\-post\-only | \-\-no\-post\-only"
Optional. Enable or disable post\-only execution.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "batch"
Place 1\-50 orders; \-\-orders @file.json.
.br
RPC: mm_placeOrders. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-orders ORDERS"
Required. JSON order array or @FILE; an object containing an orders array is
also accepted.

.SS "modify"
Modify an order; quantity is the new total, remaining is the new remainder.
.br
RPC: mm_modifyOrder. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-order\-id ID"
Required. Order ID returned by the desk.
.TP
.B "\-\-price AMOUNT"
Optional. Raw integer price.
.TP
.B "\-\-quantity AMOUNT"
Optional. Raw integer total quantity.
.TP
.B "\-\-remaining NONNEGATIVE"
Optional. New remaining quantity; zero is allowed.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "cancel"
Cancel one order.
.br
RPC: mm_cancelOrder. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-order\-id ID"
Required. Order ID returned by the desk.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "cancel-all"
Cancel all orders, optionally limited to one book.
.br
RPC: mm_cancelAll. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-book STR"
Optional. Order book identifier.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "open-orders"
List live orders.
.br
RPC: mm_openOrders. Scope: any.
.TP
.B "\-\-book STR"
Optional. Order book identifier.

.SS "order"
Get an order and its fills.
.br
RPC: mm_getOrder. Scope: any.
.TP
.B "\-\-order\-id ID"
Required. Order ID returned by the desk.

.SS "orders"
List order history; from is inclusive and to exclusive, in Unix milliseconds.
.br
RPC: mm_listOrders. Scope: any.
.TP
.B "\-\-book STR"
Optional. Order book identifier.
.TP
.B "\-\-from UINT"
Optional. Inclusive lower timestamp bound in Unix milliseconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-to UINT"
Optional. Exclusive upper timestamp bound in Unix milliseconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-state STR"
Optional. Server\-side state filter.
.TP
.B "\-\-limit UINT"
Optional. Maximum number of records.
.TP
.B "\-\-offset UINT"
Optional. Number of records to skip.

.SS "request"
Get a request result.
.br
RPC: mm_getRequest. Scope: any.
.TP
.B "\-\-pool\-request\-id ID"
Required. Pool request ID returned by the desk.

.SS "requests"
List request history.
.br
RPC: mm_listRequests. Scope: any.
.TP
.B "\-\-book STR"
Optional. Order book identifier.
.TP
.B "\-\-from UINT"
Optional. Inclusive lower timestamp bound in Unix milliseconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-to UINT"
Optional. Exclusive upper timestamp bound in Unix milliseconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-state STR"
Optional. Server\-side state filter.
.TP
.B "\-\-limit UINT"
Optional. Maximum number of records.
.TP
.B "\-\-offset UINT"
Optional. Number of records to skip.

.SS "balances"
Get desk balances.
.br
RPC: mm_balances. Scope: any.
No parameters.

.SS "deposits"
List deposit records.
.br
RPC: mm_deposits. Scope: any.
No parameters.

.SS "withdraw"
Withdraw to your own Cura account address.
.br
RPC: mm_withdraw. Scope: withdraw.
.TP
.B "\-\-token TOKEN"
Required. Asset address or configured asset name.
.TP
.B "\-\-amount AMOUNT"
Required. Positive raw integer amount.
.TP
.B "\-\-to STR"
Required. Owner's Cura account address.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "withdrawals"
List withdrawal records.
.br
RPC: mm_withdrawals. Scope: any.
No parameters.

.SS "algo-place"
Create a TWAP / VWAP schedule; times are Unix milliseconds.
.br
RPC: mm_placeAlgo. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-book STR"
Required. Order book identifier.
.TP
.B "\-\-side BUY|SELL"
Required. buy or sell.
.TP
.B "\-\-quantity AMOUNT"
Required. Raw integer total quantity.
.TP
.B "\-\-limit\-price AMOUNT"
Required. Worst acceptable slice price as a raw integer.
.TP
.B "\-\-start UINT"
Optional. Schedule start in Unix milliseconds; defaults to now.
.TP
.B "\-\-end UINT"
Required. Schedule end in Unix milliseconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-interval\-ms UINT"
Required. Positive slice interval in milliseconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-kind TWAP|VWAP"
Required. twap or vwap.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "algo-cancel"
Cancel an algorithmic order.
.br
RPC: mm_cancelAlgo. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-parent\-id ID"
Required. Algorithmic order ID returned by the desk.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "algo-pause"
Pause an algorithmic order.
.br
RPC: mm_pauseAlgo. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-parent\-id ID"
Required. Algorithmic order ID returned by the desk.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "algo-resume"
Resume an algorithmic order.
.br
RPC: mm_resumeAlgo. Scope: trade.
.TP
.B "\-\-parent\-id ID"
Required. Algorithmic order ID returned by the desk.
.TP
.B "\-\-ts UINT"
Optional. Unix milliseconds; filled automatically when omitted.

.SS "algo"
Get an algorithmic order and its slices.
.br
RPC: mm_getAlgo. Scope: any.
.TP
.B "\-\-parent\-id ID"
Required. Algorithmic order ID returned by the desk.

.SH ERRORS
A result with status rejected is a business rejection even when the
JSON-RPC request succeeded. Acceptance does not prove execution or settlement.
.PP
Unauthorized (-32001) requires authentication again. Stale timestamp
(-32002) requires checking the clock. Rate limited (-32003) requires
reducing request frequency. not_implemented, not_ready, internal, and
not_found identify service-side failures. insufficient_balance refers
to the desk's available balance.
.PP
Requests are not automatically retried. A disconnected or timed-out
write may have executed; inspect orders, requests, withdrawals, or algorithm
state before deciding to resubmit. Reconnection does not replay commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MM_DESK_URL
Default WebSocket endpoint; overridden by --url.
.TP
.B MM_DESK_PYTHON
Python executable used by the launcher; default is python3.
.TP
.BR MANPAGER , " PAGER"
Used by the system man viewer according to its normal precedence.
.SH FILES
Files are relative to the application directory unless otherwise stated.
.TP
.B mm-desk.1
This man(1) manual page.
.TP
.B markets.json
Testnet trading pair parameters, keyed by desk book. Includes source and date.
.TP
.B assets.json
Asset address, name, and decimal precision registry. Restart after changes.
Known assets display their names followed by the complete address in
parentheses.
Formatting affects output only; requests retain raw addresses and integers.
.TP
.B desk_networks.json
Desk endpoint to chain RPC, chain ID, pool owner and spot contract mapping.
.TP
.B accounts.json
Public chain-owner associations scoped by endpoint and public API key.
Read on each login. Contains no private seeds.
.TP
.B MANUAL.md
Extended reference document for reading in a Markdown viewer.
.TP
.B EXAMPLES.md
Separate command examples and walkthroughs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful command completion or a help request.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime validation, connection, query, or RPC failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid startup arguments or a business rejection in command mode.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by the user.
.SH NOTES
The simulator checks protocol interactions and signatures, not live matching,
settlement, timed deadman cancellation, or actual algorithm execution.
.PP
The application does not persist seeds, signatures, JWTs, or command history
to its own logs. Requested results, including gateway JWTs, are printed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR less (1)
